\details{
The binary upload transport is the only bulk-write implementation. \code{bulk_transport} is not supported. Encoded batches are capped at 128 MiB, and batches that exceed this limit are automatically retried with fewer rows before transmission. Upload is transactional unless the connection already has an explicit transaction; incomplete exchanges invalidate the connection. SQL types include NVARCHAR(MAX), DATE, DATETIME2, BIGINT, and VARBINARY(MAX). Factor columns are stored as character; appending factor columns produces a warning. For exact decimals, use a suitable \code{field.types} override and character input. For per-batch timings, set \code{options(RSqlClientNET.bulk_profile = TRUE)}. \code{table_lock} defaults to TRUE for each write and can be disabled per operation; it is not a persistent connection option; it does not guarantee minimal logging (recovery model, indexes, table state and other SQL Server conditions matter). Local temporary tables require the same connection on subsequent reads.
